", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Non-count nouns are an amount. They are always singular.<br /><span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Example: water &nbsp &nbsp  some water </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You use <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> some </span> with count nouns to talk about the number of items.<br /><span class=\\\"italic\\\">Example: There are some tomatoes. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You use <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> some </span> with non-count nouns to talk about the amount of an item.<br /><span class=\\\"italic\\\">Example: There is some sugar. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You use <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> any </span> with count and non-count in negative sentences and questions. <br /><span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Example: Are there any olives? No, there aren't any olives. </span><br /><span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Example: Is there any coffee? No, there isn't any. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pepper"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a green, red or yellow vegetable with a round shape"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sweet red peppers are great on pizza!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn1le05ob02aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear in a lunchroom."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "knife"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a long flat instrument for cutting"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This knife is not sharp. I can't cut my apple. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn1le05ob02aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fridge"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an electric appliance that keeps